### The Super Keyword
-- if you any thing acess  from parent variable. we can use super keyword.
-- the super keyword is used in a subclass to refer to the immediate parent class. 
-- it allow acess to the parent class variables, methods and constructors espacially when there is a naming conflict or when reusing the parent class behaviours

*** CODE ***
class Parent {
    int value = 100;
    Parent() {
        System.out.println("Parent constructor called");
    }
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Parent display method");
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    int value = 200;
    Child() {
        super(); // calls Parent constructor
        System.out.println("Child constructor called");
    }
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Child display method");
        super.display(); // calls Parent method
    }
    void showValues() {
        System.out.println("Child value: " + value);
        System.out.println("Parent value: " + super.value); // access parent variable
    }
}
public class SuperKeywordDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Child obj = new Child();
        System.out.println("-----");
        obj.display();
        System.out.println("-----");
        obj.showValues();
    }
}
Output:-
Parent constructor called
Child constructor called
-----
Child display method
Parent display method
-----
